A pinned source identifies a repository, a full commit SHA, and a path.
The [code-snippets design brief](/lore/code-snippets) reads that source from local Git objects.
[`git show`](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-show) documents object inspection.

The proposed snippet keeps its pinned text.
Source drift compares only the selected pinned lines with HEAD.
Source drift reports a warning, not replacement text or a failed build.

Keep HEAD out of the immutable snippet cache.
The cache key identifies the pinned source.
A separate diagnostic observes source drift.

If a shallow clone lacks the object, tell the author to fetch history.
Do not fetch it during content generation.

This boundary keeps [build-time work](/lore/build-time-work-stays-out-of-requests) local.
The configured registry follows [ports and adapters](/lore/hexagonal-architecture).

See [the glossary](/glossary) for pinned source and source drift.
